# Plain-CSS Dashboard System

- Keep the dashboard on the existing plain-CSS path. Do not introduce Tailwind, Aceternity, CSS-in-JS, or a component library for routine polish.
- Prefer shared CSS custom properties in `src/styles.css` for recurring colors, borders, muted text, surfaces, chips, and density values.
- Keep module CSS focused on layout and module-specific composition. Reuse shared tokens before adding new hardcoded colors.
- Preserve the current visual language: dark glass surfaces, subtle gradient borders, radial glow accents, position-tinted player context, and compact information density.
- For shared UI patterns, consolidate selectors or tokens first; only add new React abstractions when CSS alone would create duplication or unclear ownership.
- Keep Draft Room, Team Tracker, and player tiles visually consistent. When changing one pattern, check the related module for matching card, chip, metric, and scroll-panel treatment.
- Favor small, reviewable visual passes. Avoid broad rewrites unless the issue explicitly calls for a larger redesign.
